// Slicing a string with a negative stride fails. The operand `c` stays behind
// the assignment that it reads and drops every event, so the operand behind it
// must not move in front of it and slice `x`. Only `y == 1` moves.
from {x: "abc", y: 1}
c = random() < 0
where c and x.slice(stride=-1) == "" and y == 1
